{
  "dom_id": "step-e7886",
  "name": "Example: Finding the Parametric Equations of a Vertical Hyperbola Given Algebraically",
  "problem": "What are the parametric equations of the hyperbola $\\dfrac{y^2}{9} - \\dfrac{x^2}{25} = 1?$",
  "worked_solution": "The parametric equations of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{y^2}{a^2} - \\frac{x^2}{b^2} = 1\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\nx = b\\tan{t}, \\quad y = a\\sec{t}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a = \\sqrt{9} = 3$ and $b = \\sqrt{25} = 5.$ Therefore, the parametric equations are\n\n$$\nx = 5\\tan{t}, \\quad y = 3\\sec{t}.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
